{# narrative_engine/plot_slot — who, where or what fills one slot of a step.
   Asked by PlotPlanning for each slot with more than one candidate, and
   by PickAgent for the agent. The answer is a candidate key, c1 onward.
   Receives: mastermind { name }, scheme, step (the step's sentence with
     each unfilled slot shown as its name in brackets), purpose (what the
     step is for in the plan), slot (the name being filled), kind (person,
     place or thing), options [{ key, line }].
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state scheme ]
{{ mastermind.name }} is working toward this: {{ scheme }}
[ end state ]

[ state step ]
{{ step }}
{{ purpose }}
[ end state ]

[ question pick choice ]
{% if kind == "place" %}Where should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else if kind == "thing" %}What should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else %}Who should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`? Prefer the person this scheme is plainly about, if they are on the list and the step is about them.{% endif %}
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.line }}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
